  "faqQ1": "Where are my words kept?",
  "@faqQ1": {"description": "FAQ question 1."},
  "faqA1": "Only on this phone, in VocabNote's own private storage. There is no account and no server. To keep a copy anywhere else, make a backup.",
  "@faqA1": {"description": "FAQ answer 1."},
  "faqQ2": "How do I move my words to a new phone?",
  "@faqQ2": {"description": "FAQ question 2."},
  "faqA2": "Go to Settings → Backup & restore → Export backup, and save the file somewhere your new phone can reach. Then install VocabNote there and choose Import backup.",
  "@faqA2": {"description": "FAQ answer 2."},
  "faqQ3": "Does VocabNote need the internet?",
  "@faqQ3": {"description": "FAQ question 3."},
  "faqA3": "No. Everything works offline. Only Look up uses the internet, and all it sends is the word you are looking up.",
  "@faqA3": {"description": "FAQ answer 3."},
  "faqQ4": "Why does the voice sound like a computer?",
  "@faqQ4": {"description": "FAQ question 4."},
  "faqA4": "It is your phone's own text-to-speech: a good guide to stress and vowels, but not a native speaker. You can change the voice, speed and pitch in Settings → Pronunciation.",
  "@faqA4": {"description": "FAQ answer 4. The honest line about TTS (DATA-SOURCES 4)."},
  "faqQ5": "My phone has no British English voice.",
  "@faqQ5": {"description": "FAQ question 5."},
  "faqA5": "Add one in your phone's settings, under Text-to-speech on Android or Spoken Content on iPhone. Until then, VocabNote uses the closest voice it can find.",
  "@faqA5": {"description": "FAQ answer 5."},
  "faqQ6": "How do I type IPA symbols?",
  "@faqQ6": {"description": "FAQ question 6."},
  "faqA6": "Tap into an IPA field and a row of symbols appears above the keyboard. Tap a symbol to add it where the cursor is.",
  "@faqA6": {"description": "FAQ answer 6."},
  "faqQ7": "What is IPA?",
  "@faqQ7": {"description": "FAQ question 7."},
  "faqA7": "The International Phonetic Alphabet: one symbol for each sound, so a pronunciation is written down exactly - /kɒf/ rather than \"coff\".",
  "@faqA7": {"description": "FAQ answer 7."},
  "faqQ8": "How do highlights work?",
  "@faqQ8": {"description": "FAQ question 8."},
  "faqA8": "Open a word, tap Edit IPA highlights, choose the symbols you struggle with and pick a colour. A short label, like \"lips rounder\", helps too.",
  "@faqA8": {"description": "FAQ answer 8."},
  "faqQ9": "How does practice decide what comes back?",
  "@faqQ9": {"description": "FAQ question 9."},
  "faqA9": "Each word sits in a box. Know it and it moves up a box and waits longer; miss it and it comes back later the same day. You can change the gaps in Settings → Practice.",
  "@faqA9": {"description": "FAQ answer 9."},
  "faqQ10": "What's the difference between Daily review and Quick test?",
  "@faqQ10": {"description": "FAQ question 10."},
  "faqA10": "Daily review shows the words that are due, and your answers decide when each comes back. A quick test is just for practice: it never changes that.",
  "@faqA10": {"description": "FAQ answer 10."},
  "faqQ11": "I deleted a word by mistake.",
  "@faqQ11": {"description": "FAQ question 11."},
  "faqA11": "Tap Undo on the message that appears straight away. After that, importing a backup made before you deleted it will bring it back.",
  "@faqA11": {"description": "FAQ answer 11."},
  "faqQ12": "Where do the definitions come from?",
  "@faqQ12": {"description": "FAQ question 12."},
  "faqA12": "From Wiktionary, through FreeDictionaryAPI.com, shared under CC BY-SA 4.0. Offline pronunciations come from the CMU Pronouncing Dictionary. Settings → Data sources & licences has the details.",
  "@faqA12": {"description": "FAQ answer 12."},
